## Always

- Write or update the contract before the code; code, clients and mocks follow it.
- Use the shared naming, response and error shape; reference the one error envelope, never redefine it ([01]({{ref_01}})).
- Idempotency keys are claimed atomically, a changed payload under the same key is rejected, and a timeout is an unknown outcome ([01]({{ref_01}})).
- State who may call each endpoint and which data it may touch ([03]({{ref_03}})).
- Prefer adding over modifying. Removing, renaming or changing the meaning or observable behavior of anything is breaking: give a compatible path and a deprecation note, flag it for the version bump, and keep one live version ([04]({{ref_04}})).
- Say whether evidence ran against a mock or the real endpoint.

